

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 3

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU








  Quote of the Week:

  Philotheus, Russian monk and scholar, in a letter to Czar Basil III in 
1510:
  "The church of old Rome fell because of its heresy; the Second Rome, 
Constantinople, was sacked by infidels; but now the church of your mighty 
realm, the Third Rome, shines brighter than the sun, and a Fourth Rome there 
shall not be."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season, Uga-Buga Makumb prepared to quench 
his thirst for adventure.  Lallipugh was magically charmed by 
Uga-Buga Makumb.  Uga-Buga Makumb sank his fangs into Lallipugh and drained 
all his blood.  Lallipugh changed to Undead alignment!
  In early summer, Odysseus was magically charmed by Uga-Buga Makumb.  
Uga-Buga Makumb sank his fangs into Odysseus and drained his blood.  
Odysseus changed to Undead alignment!  Uga-Buga Makumb's experience improved 
his prowess in Necromancy.
  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in Necromancy.  At levels 5 and 
up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, and 
the number of spells you can cast in Necromancy is capped at 3 Action, 2 
Combat.  The effects of the "Skeletal Armies", "Plague" and "Hand of Death" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this 
exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".

  With the advent of the late summer season, Uga-Buga Makumb cruised over to 
the Icaria Sea.
  During fall, Amalric was magically charmed by Uga-Buga Makumb.  
Uga-Buga Makumb sank his fangs into Amalric and sucked up all his blood.  
Amalric changed to Evil alignment!
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb travelled to 
Mare Tarkium.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Kokocala (#10) left Hollabrand to attend a reunion of his old regiment in 
Mare Ionium.


  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 58 gold in revenue.  18 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 260th Garrison, the 268th Garrison, the 269th Bowmen, the 
272nd Dragons and the 277th Eagles trained well and improved in quality.  33 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was left with 14 
gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Montgomery, Squire to Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Guerin prepared to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He cast a Skeletal Army spell and the 124th Skeletal Dragons 
arose from the graves of the dead!
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Tao-Li recruited the 272nd 
Dragons from among the people of Mare Tarkium, to serve under Guerin.
  Guerin boldly marched his forces into Falkenheim (#1106).
  With the advent of the late summer season Guerin failed in his ineffectual 
attempt to cast a Skeletal Army spell.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Guerin tried a Bless spell, but bungled 
it.
  Tao-Li announced a plea for volunteers in Falkenheim and was able to form 
the 277th Eagles to fight for Guerin.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  Guerin marched on Hollabrand (#1206) 
with his command.  Viewing the northeastern horizon, a man can see a Forest 
province known as the Falkland Sea (#1305).  It is said that Isis is the 
ruler there.  It is known to be populated by Elves.  Their Elven warriors 
array themselves as Bowmen and Fleet.  East of here lies the poor province 
of the Ark Royal Sea (#1306), ruled by Dracona.  It is said to be a Mountain 
province occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish warriors prefer to array themselves 
in the style of Legion and Warg Riders.  To the southeast lies a Mountain 
province called Jutland (#1307), populated by Orcs.  It is ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  Their Orcish warriors prefer to fight in 
the style of Bowmen.  Guerin was informed by some peasants of a feature in 
Hollabrand previously unknown to us, a Glade (#126) inhabited by the Dryad.  
What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Dryad is a weak female tree 
spite who makes her home in the forested wilderness.  She usually prefers to 
be left alone.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Forest province of Hollabrand, a land defended by the forces 
of Kokocala.  Guerin commanded the invading armies.  The defending forces 
were commanded by Kokocala.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Hollabrand (1206):

  209th    124th/S  
  Wargs    Dragons  
    01     01 
                    
  241st     110th   
  Bowmen    Bowmen  
 }}}01}}}  }}}01}}} 
                    
