  Bowmen    Bowmen  
 }}}01}}}  }}}01}}} 
--------------------
    10        10    
 132nd/A   133rd/A  
  Legion   Chariots 
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 272nd Dragons, the 109th Heavy Cavalry and the 277th 
Eagles in reserve.  Guerin stood ready at the head of his thousands.  
Kokocala led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The two armies strived mightily for the high ground, and 
Guerin obtained an advantage by arriving there before the enemy.  On the 
other hand his meticulous tactical plans failed to work out, and his men 
fought with a slight tactical disadvantage.
  The Dragons Guerin led were rendered worthless by their poor relations 
with Guerin.  He could make almost no use of the Eagles, who virtually 
ignored his commands.
  Out on the left flank, the Veteran 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 132nd 
Legion.  The 241st Bowmen flanked the enemy and attacked with full force.  
The 272nd Dragons soared over the 132nd Legion and attacked them.  The 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen fought the 132nd Legion and easily crushed them.
  On the right outside flank, the Crack 240th Bowmen were arrayed against 
the 133rd Chariots.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 133rd 
Chariots and attacked without mercy.  The 240th Bowmen fought the 133rd 
Chariots and smashed their skulls as if they were eggplants.
  The host of Guerin crushed the army of Kokocala's morale with one last 
push.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen demolished the 132nd Legion.  The 240th 
Bowmen slew the 133rd Chariots almost to a man.
  Guerin's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered the province 
of Hollabrand.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we can raise 
the ranking of the 241st Bowmen to Crack, its men having displayed 
especially admirable elan.  The 110th Bowmen proved its mettle during the 
fight and we now rate it a Veteran unit.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Guerin


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring, and Teleko made ready to carry out his urgent 
assignments.  He enlisted enough men in the Mermaid Sea to form the 260th 
Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Teleko announced a plea for 
volunteers in the Mermaid Sea and was able to form the 269th Bowmen and the 
270th Bowmen to fight for Teleko.
  In late summer, Teleko moved into the Icaria Sea (#1007) with his 
redoubtable army.

  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded 
the Icaria Sea, hoping to conquer that province owned by Amalric and made up 
of extensive Forests.  Teleko commanded the invading armies.  The defending 
forces were led by Amalric.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Icaria Sea (1007):

  270th   
  Bowmen  
