  DEFENDING ARMY

  Teleko stood determinedly at the head of his thousands.  Amalric marched 
with his loyal troops, jaws set in grim determination.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Teleko took a chance on infiltrating some scouts behind 
enemy lines to set fire to their armament wagons, and the plan succeeded 
completely.  Further, in this chess match, Teleko appeared to gain the 
tactical edge.

  Across the entire front, the 96th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 112th 
Heavy Cavalry.  The 269th Bowmen and the 270th Bowmen flanked the 
undermanned enemy and attacked with full strength.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen 
battled the 112th Heavy Cavalry and mowed them down like weeds.
  The forces of Teleko broke through the lines of their opposition and were 
victorious.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen scattered the 112th Heavy Cavalry in 
all directions.
  The Icaria Sea was overrun by the forces of Teleko.  The battle affected 
the quality of our forces:  the 96th Skeletal Bowmen was greatly buoyed by 
the victory.  We now designate it a proud Veteran unit.  The 270th Bowmen 
fought determinedly during the battle and came through with flying colors.  
We can now rank it an Average unit.
  In fall, Teleko failed in his attempt to cast a Skeletal Army spell.
  The fall cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Teleko moved into the 
Near-Beer Sea (#907) with his redoubtable army.  Turning to the southwest, 
one can see a Mountain area, which is known as the Iceberg Sea (#808).  It 
is populated by Humans and Alain rules there.  Their Human fighters 
traditionally array themselves in the style of Legion and Chariots.  West of 
here is the Third Sea (#807), a Forest area ruled by Presto, where Elves 
dwell.  Their Elven warriors fight in the style of Axemen.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of the Near-Beer Sea,
a Forest area owned by Elmer (#58).  Teleko commanded the invading armies.  
The defending forces were commanded by Elmer.  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Near-Beer Sea (0907):

  269th             
  Bowmen            
