--------------------
    58        58    
  98th/A    99th/A  
 Phalanx    Wargs   
                    
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Teleko marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Elmer 
led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  No luck or misfortune of noteworthy importance affected 
the general course of the battle.  In this perilous chess match, Teleko 
seemed to gain the tactical upper hand.

  Out on the left wing, the Veteran 96th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 98th 
Phalanx.  The 269th Bowmen flanked the enemy and charged in with full 
strength.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 98th Phalanx and smashed 
their heads as if they were eggshells.
  On the right outside flank, the 270th Bowmen faced the 99th Warg Riders.  
On this field, the men of the 270th Bowmen had lost sleep because of the 
local food and became slightly ill.  They entered battle at a minor 
disadvantage.  The 270th Bowmen fought the 99th Warg Riders and fought them 
to a standstill.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Teleko as they broke 
through the lines at a critical moment.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen destroyed 
the 98th Phalanx.
  The Near-Beer Sea was overrun by Teleko's men in a bloody campaign.  The 
battle affected the quality of our forces:  we could not have been more 
pleased with the elan of the 270th Bowmen, and we have elevated its rating 
to Veteran.  The 99th Warg Riders were unable to retreat and were disbanded 
into the population.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Melantheus enlisted enough men in the Virgo Sea to form the 
268th Garrison for the army of the provincial garrison commander.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He invented nothing 
worthy of note in his sagely researches.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer arrived.  Melantheus 
tried to practice his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He 
discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely researches.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  Melantheus discovered nothing 
in his sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the early winter season Melantheus invented nothing in 
his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I rode into Mare Tarkium.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I recruited the 272nd Dragons 
from among the people of Mare Tarkium, to serve under Guerin.
  In late summer, I travelled to Falkenheim.
  With the coming of the fall season I announced a plea for volunteers in 
Falkenheim and was able to form the 277th Eagles to fight for Guerin.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  I travelled to the Jellyfish Sea.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the early summer season I journeyed to the Virgo Sea.  
In my travels, I saw no monsters.
  In late summer, I was tutored in Sageness by Melantheus.  I tried to 
practice my Sageness, but the task was beyond my ability.  I discovered 
nothing in my sagely researches.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  I was instructed in Sageness 
by Melantheus.  I practiced enthusiastically and improved my ability in 
Sageness.  I discovered nothing worthy of note in my sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early winter season I invented nothing worthy of 
note in my sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  During early winter, Amalric moved into Mare Tarkium.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Amalric


From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I rode into the 
Virgo Sea.  During my travels, I was crossing an open field when a 
Renegade Illusionist spotted me from a distance.  I hailed 
the Renegade Illusionist with respectful words, and combat was averted.

  With the coming of the fall season I was tutored in the art of Sageness by 
Melantheus.  I practiced for many weeks and my skill in Sageness increased.  
I discovered nothing valuable in my sagely researches.
  I heard a rumor telling of a perilous feature in the Shark Sea (#908), a 
Loch where dwells the Elasmosaurus.  The Loch is reputed to contain the Helm 
of Psychic Projection.
  During early winter, I discovered nothing worthy of note in my sagely 
experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


