GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT


Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In early summer, a conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Erg Iguidi, a 
Mountain area ruled by Saladin (#14).  Babba Sissoko (#0) was in command of 
the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by Saladin (#14).  Erg 
Iguidi was overrun by Babba Sissoko (#0)'s forces in a bloody campaign.

  In fall, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango ordered an invasion force into 
the adjacent Plain province of the Shark Sea, owned by Arnulf (#19).  
Babba Sissoko (#0) commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces 
were commanded by Arnulf (#19).  The Shark Sea was overrun by the forces of 
Babba Sissoko (#0).
  In early winter, Rainulf (#25) flew into the Shark Sea.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached level 5 in Necromancy.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Necromancy is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Skeletal Armies", "Plague" and 
"Hand of Death" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will 
still determine who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, your 
characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".


END MOVES REPORT



